13_Nightmares said:
I decided to test the plugin on a large map and immediately discovered a compatibility error with "Galv Event Spawner". Regardless of whether there is a notetag.
Spoiler:
error
View attachment 344013
Click to expand...
@NinefoldSpirit
Please remove the forwarding of your note/meta attributes in initialize, there's too much risk that it breaks with other plugins.
Code:
// upper block was removed

const Alias_SkipUpdate_Game_Event_update = Game_Event.prototype.update;
Game_Event.prototype.update = function() {
    if(!this.event() || !this.event().meta || !this.event().meta.SkipUpdate){
        Alias_SkipUpdate_Game_Event_update.call(this);
    }
}
When it still breaks, then you can blame Galv/Visustella/any other plugin creator for not processing notetags when cloning events

I had contemplating adding the meta data to the event that way, but I didn't notice that .event() existed, only that .note and .meta seemed to be missing from the event's data itself.  So this is good to know, thanks.
I'll push an update to this and remove it as it's no longer necessary.
I've done very little testing with this so I don't know what it's interaction with duplication from other event plugins.
